
Molecular Diagnostics Market to Reach USD 108.7 Billion by 2034 
The Global Molecular Diagnostics Market size was valued at USD 45.6 billion in 2025. The market is projected to grow from USD 50.3 billion in 2026 to USD 108.7 billion by 2034, exhibiting a CAGR of 10.2% during the forecast period.
Molecular diagnostics encompass advanced analytical techniques that detect and measure biological markers at the molecular level, enabling precise disease diagnosis, prognosis, and personalized treatment strategies. These diagnostic methods leverage technologies such as polymerase chain reaction (PCR), next‑generation sequencing (NGS), fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH), and microarray analysis to identify genetic mutations, infectious pathogens, and biomarkers associated with cancers, inherited disorders, and chronic diseases. The integration of molecular diagnostics into clinical workflows has revolutionized healthcare by facilitating early detection, targeted therapies, and improved patient outcomes.
